### KYC API — runnable examples for the VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client / Visual Studio.
### Start the stack first:  docker compose up --build   (see docs/getting-started.md)

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Liveness (is the process up?)
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness (do SQL Server and Redis answer?)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### Register a customer (201 Created + Location header)
# @name createCustomer
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ada",
  "lastName": "Lovelace",
  "dob": "1990-05-17",
  "customerAddress": {
    "street": "12 St James's Square",
    "city": "London",
    "state": "England",
    "country": "United Kingdom",
    "zipCode": "SW1Y 4JH"
  }
}

### Read the customer back (uses the id from the response above)
@customerId = {{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
GET {{host}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}

### List all customers
GET {{host}}/api/customers

### Register in the background through Hangfire (202 Accepted + job id)
POST {{host}}/api/customers/async
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Grace",
  "lastName": "Hopper",
  "dob": "1985-12-09"
}

### Validation failure (400 application/problem+json listing FirstName and Dob)
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Turing",
  "dob": "2999-01-01"
}

### Unknown customer (404 application/problem+json)
GET {{host}}/api/customers/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### OpenAPI document (Development / Docker only)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
